{"chunk_id": "b419486e3097", "text": "Krishna (Kesava) reveals a terrifying divine manifestation in the Kuru court after Duryodhana\u2019s defiance. From his blazing body emerge countless gods, celestial beings, weapons, and heroes, while flames and sparks radiate from every pore. Most kings shut their eyes in fear, but sages and a few wise elders are granted divine sight to behold the cosmic form. After the earth trembles and celestial drums sound, Krishna withdraws the vision and departs the court. Dhritarashtra insists he sought peace, but Krishna points out that Duryodhana rejected all counsel. He then visits Kunti, recounts the failed diplomacy, and asks what message he should carry to the Pandavas. Kunti urges Yudhishthira to remember his Kshatriya duty and not let passive virtue prevent rightful action.\nKrishna reveals a terrifying cosmic form in the Kuru court, departs unharmed, then informs Kunti, who urges Yudhishthira to fulfill his warrior duty.\nThemes: divine revelation, Krishna's cosmic form, failed diplomacy, Kshatriya duty, inevitability of war", "vector": [-0.002235276624560356, -0.011863256804645061, 0.0005932468338869512, 0.015598234720528126, -0.0010235921945422888, 0.011245238594710827, -0.02720622345805168, -0.024237049743533134, -0.008994847536087036, -0.010170425288379192, 0.012971658259630203, 0.0011100810952484608, 0.0023780253250151873, 0.01888985186815262, -0.014214412309229374, 0.006240637507289648, 0.043959882110357285, -0.017949389293789864, 0.028563175350427628, -0.02380712516605854, 0.004161544609814882, -0.00474933348596096, -0.0037349776830524206, 0.014227846637368202, -0.018231527879834175, 0.022826356813311577, 0.019010769203305244, -0.0325668565928936, 0.011298979632556438, -0.010889207012951374, -0.008437287993729115, 0.005891323089599609, 0.008726144209504128, -0.011735622771084309, -0.03178761526942253, 0.025204382836818695, 0.011265391483902931, -0.025204382836818695, 0.009102328680455685, -0.006610104814171791, 0.00251741